WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.370
Charge a capacitor to 20 volts,
then take the battery away.

2
00:00:04.420 --> 00:00:06.260
Connect it across a coil.

3
00:00:06.310 --> 00:00:11.690
Nothing else: no battery, and in
this ideal circuit, no resistance.

4
00:00:11.740 --> 00:00:14.210
The charge doesn't simply drain away.

5
00:00:14.260 --> 00:00:16.990
The capacitor charges up the opposite way,

6
00:00:17.040 --> 00:00:19.760
then back again, over and over.

7
00:00:19.810 --> 00:00:22.970
With no resistance, it never dies down.

8
00:00:23.020 --> 00:00:25.760
Why does the charge swing back and forth?

9
00:00:25.810 --> 00:00:28.150
In this mission, you'll follow one cycle,

10
00:00:28.200 --> 00:00:29.640
step by step.

11
00:00:29.690 --> 00:00:33.740
Then you'll find that the charge obeys
the same kind of equation as a mass on

12
00:00:33.790 --> 00:00:34.980
a spring.

13
00:00:35.030 --> 00:00:38.920
Your mission: explain why the
charge swings back and forth.
